    <div class="kicker">Problem Definition</div>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 class="section-title">Portal work was manual, repetitive, and easy to get wrong</h2>
        <p>A lot of RFx work happens inside vendor "portals" - a custom procurement sites where an RFP gets posted. The only way in is to log in, read every question, and copy it out somewhere you can actually work. This time wastedsetup, and for teams juggling dozens of live RFPs, it could eat the first hour of a session before anyone wrote a real answer.</p>
        <p>Customers told us this plainly, call after call:</p>
        <blockquote>“The SmartScan feature in the portal was so, so much easier than uploading a document to Loopio or having to manually copy and paste questions to a project.”<cite>Proposal Content Manager, a healthcare data and analytics company</cite></blockquote>
        <blockquote>“It's great to see the portal import process being made streamlined and made more automated.”<cite>Proposals team member, a benefits administration technology company</cite></blockquote>
        <p>We didn't need a better copy-paste workaround. We needed the portal itself to become an entry point into Loopio.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-card">
