    <div class="prose">
      <p>I ran this like an actual research program, not a feature ticket. We started with an internal alpha with our sales and customer success teams: they talk to customers about these portals every day, so I could get fast, well-informed feedback before running a full external cycle. From there we moved into a wider customer beta, then general release.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ai-box">
      <div class="label">AI in the process</div>
      <p>Claude Cowork took my interview notes, survey responses, and months of call transcripts and found themes in a fraction of the time a manual pass would've taken. Claude Design helped me push through wireframe directions fast, especially the hardest problem here: fitting a dense RFx question, and a confident answer, into a few hundred pixels of sidebar. Work that used to take half a day, wireframing especially, dropped to about 30 minutes. Every microcopy draft Cowork helped write still went through real usability testing before it shipped.</p>
    </div>
